RDS= relational database service that uses SQL
database used by AWS: postgres,mysql,mariadb,oracle,microsoft SQL,IBM DB2,Aurora
RDS:
  1) automated
  2) continious backup and restore
  3) Multi AZ setup for DR
  4) scaling vertical and horizontal: used maximum storage threshold which is the limit for DB storage
  5) storage backed by EBS

RDS read replicas: scale the amount of reads(select statements) you can do on the database. Can do this in the same AZ,Cross AZ and cross region and does this async.
This works by making a replica of the production db and you it for the reporting application.
for multi AZ: it automatically fails over to increase availability by using the same dns name. And zero downtime when failing over

RDS custom: used for oracle and microsoft SQL. Access to the underlying database an OS. During doing it de-activate automation mode.

Amazon Aurora:  proprietary technology from AWS, supports PostGres and MySQL, aws cloud optimized, storage automatically grows in increments of 10 GB when it smaller then 256 TB.
